203 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 526 0 R
/E ( Graph Neural Networks \(GNNs\) are a novel deep learning technique specifically designed to operate on graph-structured data. They generalize traditional neural networks to graphs by performing learning algorithms that aggregate and propagate information over nodes and edges in a graph.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
204 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 527 0 R
/E (They come as useful in for modeling complex relationships in social networks, where news, users, and interactions naturally form graph structures, overcoming the limitation of previous ML approaches that assumed news items were independent.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
205 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
