/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
207 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 529 0 R
/E (They came in as an extension of RNNs to graph structured data. Their mechanism is based on an information diffusion process where node states \(embeddings\) are iteratively updated by exchanging information with neighbours.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (   a\) How GNNs Process Graph Data?)
/E (   a\) How GNNs Process Graph Data?)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
209 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 530 0 R
/E (GNNs process graph data by passing information between nodes through their connections \(edges\).)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 531 0 R
/E ( Each node gathers information from its neighbours in a process called message passing, allowing it to learn representations based on its local structure and features. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 532 0 R
/E (This iterative information-sharing allows nodes to understand the context provided by surrounding nodes in the graph.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
